            <ArticleTitle>Evidence for the effectiveness of cardiac rehabilitation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>38-48</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cardiac rehabilitation is a relatively recent development and, though it is increasingly being recognized as an important part of comprehensive cardiac care, there remains some scepticism regarding its effectiveness and some ignorance of its potential. This article reviews the literature pertaining to the effectiveness of cardiac rehabilitation for patients with coronary heart disease (CHD).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
